      "paragraph": 1,
      "claim": "EvoTech has expanded its voluntary recall of Pro Series smartwatches to 85,000 units due to a lithium-polymer cell separator defect causing rapid overheating.",
      "quote": "EvoTech Inc. has expanded its voluntary recall of the EvoTech Pro Series smartwatch to cover 85,000 units sold between January and June after engineering tests confirmed that a separator defect in the lithium-polymer cell can cause rapid overheating during wireless charging."
    },
    {
      "doc_id": "d1",
      "paragraph": 2,
      "claim": "Thirty-eight customers reported overheating above 62°C, leading to four blister injuries and two scorched nightstands, while an interim firmware patch does not fix the underlying physical defect.",
      "quote": "The recall was initiated after thirty-eight customers reported devices reaching surface temperatures above 62°C, including four cases of minor wrist blisters and two scorched nightstands. EvoTech released an interim firmware patch that caps charging current at 50%, but regulators warn that software limits do not cure the physical battery fault."
    },
    {
      "doc_id": "d1",
      "paragraph": 4,
      "claim": "Owners must power down the smartwatches and use a support portal to request thermal return kits for a full refund or a Series 2 replacement.",
      "quote": "Owners are instructed to power down the watch immediately and request a prepaid thermal return kit through the dedicated support portal at https://recall.evotech.example/pro-series for a full refund or a redesigned Series 2 replacement."
    },
    {
      "doc_id": "d2",
      "paragraph": 1,
      "claim": "Safety agencies advise stopping use of approximately 82,000 watches following forty-one reports of battery swelling and thermal runaway.",
      "quote": "Consumer safety agencies have urged owners of EvoTech Pro Series smartwatches (model numbers ETP-40 and ETP-44) to stop wearing or charging the devices following forty-one reports of severe battery swelling and thermal runaway. Approximately 82,000 watches distributed through retail electronics chains are affected."
    },
    {
      "doc_id": "d2",
      "paragraph": 2,
      "claim": "Degraded battery cells can still overheat on high-wattage induction pads despite an over-the-air firmware temperature throttle.",
      "quote": "While EvoTech pushed an over-the-air firmware update last week intended to throttle charging temperatures, independent testing labs found that degraded cells can still overheat if left on high-wattage induction pads."
    },
    {
      "doc_id": "d2",
      "paragraph": 3,
      "claim": "Returning customers are offered a $290 refund or a voucher for an updated replacement model.",
      "quote": "Customers returning affected watches receive either a $290 purchase refund or a voucher for an updated model once hardware replacements ship next month."
    },
    {
      "doc_id": "d3",
      "paragraph": 1,
      "claim": "About 84,000 smartwatches are being recalled after contaminated cathode foil led to overheating and five reported minor skin burns.",
      "quote": "EvoTech Inc. is recalling roughly 84,000 Pro Series smartwatches after quality audits traced a cluster of overheating complaints to contaminated cathode foil in batteries assembled during the first quarter. Five minor skin burns have been logged by the company's safety hotline."
    },
    {
      "doc_id": "d3",
      "paragraph": 2,
      "claim": "Retailers have pulled stock from shelves and catalogs while the firmware limiter serves as a temporary safeguard.",
      "quote": "Retail partners have removed remaining Pro Series stock from store shelves and online catalogs. EvoTech executives stated that the interim firmware limiter is only a temporary safeguard until physical units are returned."
    },
    {
      "doc_id": "d3",
      "paragraph": 3,
      "claim": "Prepaid fire-resistant return pouches are sent to registered owners with turnaround times of seven to ten business days.",
      "quote": "Prepaid fire-resistant return pouches are being mailed to registered owners, with processing times averaging seven to ten business days."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 0.95
}

